<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Singapore</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Singapore is an island city at the southern tip of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>, on the major sea route between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-china-sea">South China Sea</a>. Founded as a British trading post in 1819, it became a key British naval base, and its fall to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 1942 was a severe blow to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya Empire</a> note its earlier role in regional maritime trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/singapore.jpg" alt="Singapore" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Government of Singapore Vector: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Singapore.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
